THIS PATCH vs UPSTREAM #32209 (the PR we would otherwise have opened)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Same idea, same placement, same slot semantics.  Ours is a SUBSET, adapted:

  scope      #32209 also ships a `_forward_trtllm` decode trim, a CUDA idle
             short-circuit in `forward_cuda`, and an eager draft-output slice.
             We take only the vote.
  base       Ours applies to v0.5.18; #32209 targets `main`.
  default    #32209 defaults the field to False, ours to True.  Its scheduler
             sets the value on every DP path; on this base the field can reach a
             non-DP forward unset, where False would refuse the graph outright.
             Permissive-by-default matches how idle ranks are already treated.
  names      Fields follow #32209 rather than carrying a local prefix, so if it
             merges this patch is a plain delete.  Those identifiers are also
             what the build script greps out of the BYTECODE to prove the patch
             landed -- see apply_sglang_dsa_patches.sh.

RE-CUT FOR v0.5.18 (previously cut against v0.5.17)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Same mechanism. Six files and six of seven dp_attn.py hunks still apply exactly
at `--fuzz=0`; only the reduction hunk changed because v0.5.18 copies the packed
tensor to `tp0_info_cpu` once and reduces that host mirror instead of calling
`.item()` repeatedly on `tp0_info`. The re-cut follows that new source shape and
adds slot 7 to the same CPU reduction. No behavior or field naming changed.

TWO DETAILS THAT WOULD MAKE THIS SILENTLY INERT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Under overlap scheduling the draft input resolves AFTER the scheduler-side
   vote, so `dsa_topk_indices` is stale and must not be read directly.  The
   predicate consults `future_dsa_topk_indices_available` -- exactly "will term 4
   hold once resolved".  An earlier revision wrongly assumed that attribute was
   absent and required eager whenever `future_indices` was set; overlap
   scheduling sets it on EVERY decode iteration, so the draft graph was refused
   100% of the time (measured 0.0%, 200/200 calls) -- degrading this patch into
   the "just disable the draft graph" workaround while passing every test.
2. Removing only the `not is_idle()` term does NOT work: it fixes the busy-rank
   iteration and breaks the idle-rank one, which matches the observed symptom of
   the failure moving earlier, into warmup.

EVIDENCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
v0.5.17, 2 x 8 MI355X, GLM-5.2-FP8 1P1D, both legs TP8 + `--dp-size 8
--enable-dp-attention` + EAGLE 3 steps / 4 draft tokens, IndexShare ON:
  unpatched  first routed request never returns (120 s timeout); all ranks parked
             in `all_gather_into_tensor` on the draft attention path.
  patched    first request 2.3 s; 256/256 requests at conc=64 (ISL 1024 / OSL
             512), accept len 2.31-4.00 against a ceiling of 4.
A green stress result alone cannot distinguish this fix from forcing the draft
path eager -- both pass every functional test.  What rules that out here is that
the accept length reaches the ceiling and the deadlock is gone: the vote must be
flipping, or the group decision would still be permissive and the hang would
remain.  On an earlier gfx950 cut the finer instrumentation was run and is worth
recording: over 2992 iterations with all 8 ranks logging, the LOCAL decision
still diverged 38 times, the ACTED-ON decision diverged 0 times, the vote changed
some rank's mind 190 times, and draft-graph usage stayed at 97.1%.

ALTERNATIVE TO THIS PATCH: turn GLM-5.2 MTP IndexShare off
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    --json-model-override-args '{"index_share_for_mtp_iteration":false}'

Rather than making the decision uniform, this removes what makes it diverge: no
seed, no divergence, no vote.  It substitutes for THIS patch and for
dsa_page_table_rows; NOT for patch 01, NOT for dsa_dp_sync.  The gfx942 recipe
takes exactly this route -- see apply_sglang_dsa_patches.sh.
Two conditions easy to miss: MTP must be on the PREFILL leg too (else the seed
never reaches decode and the setting is untested rather than tested), and that
arm was measured to conc=64, not 128.
WHY IT IS NOT THE DEFAULT HERE: it is nearly free only while IndexShare's
consumer stays disabled under PD by `should_use_dsa_fused_topk`.  Upstream #31477
("[Spec][PD] Enable fused TopK for GLM-5.2 MTP IndexShare") MERGED 2026-08-05 to
remove that limitation, and once a base carries it the override starts costing
(~3% TPOT, reported internally -- second-hand, not measured by us).  v0.5.17 does
NOT carry it: dsa/utils.py still returns `... and not pd_index_share_seed` under
its TODO.  So the override remains a good answer on this base and a dated one on
the next.

